Raise firmware-config's memory cap from 48M to 72M.

The konnect mod adds a settings section to the firmware-config page, and
every settings item's get_cmd spawns an extended-config.py subprocess (a
full python3) inside firmware-config's own cgroup. The stock 48M cap was
already within one subprocess of the ceiling on a loaded page — observed
on hardware as a CONSTRAINT_MEMCG oom-kill of firmware-config.py at
anon-rss 43.7M — so the overlay that adds an item also raises the budget
it runs in.

--- a/etc/init.d/S99firmware-config
+++ b/etc/init.d/S99firmware-config
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@
     fi

     . /usr/local/sbin/limits-helper.sh
-    limits_enter firmware-config 48M
+    limits_enter firmware-config 72M

     start-stop-daemon -S -b -m -p "$PIDFILE" -x /usr/bin/python3 -- \
         "$DAEMON" --bind "$BIND" --port "$PORT" \
